# Moods (after Avonlea; Mood first on the scene's page, Natural the default: the day goes round; a
# named mood holds its time and character; Custom once a knob is turned), Warmth (bright to mellow), Hotaru's
# Weather (Auto, Clear, Mist, Rain; on the Nature page); kept across a power-off; star glints heard
wait 800
expect scene 0
expect knob0 0
expect knob11 0
# Sakura: Natural -> Morning (lively), then on to Night (sparse, mellow; after Golden Hour)
spin K1 1
expect knob0 1
expect knob1 45
expect knob4 80
spin K1 3
expect knob0 4
expect knob1 12
expect knob11 40
# Warmth by hand (Music, KNOB 2): the mood keeps it (every mood its own tweaks; no Custom)
tap FX
tap FX
tap FX
spin K2 10
expect knob11 50
expect knob0 4
expect tweaks 16
# another mood is as it was made; back to Night: the tweak is there (Music, Key, round to Scene)
tap FX
tap FX
spin K1 2
expect knob0 0
expect knob11 0
spin K1 -1
expect resetm 4
spin K1 -1
expect knob0 4
expect resetm -1
expect knob11 50
# kept across a power-off
tap SAVE
wait 300
reboot
wait 800
expect knob0 4
expect knob11 50
expect tweaks 16
# turned past it onto "Reset Night" and left there 2 s: Night as it was made
spin K1 1
expect resetm 4
wait 2500
expect resetm -1
expect knob0 4
expect knob11 40
expect tweaks 0
# ALGORITHM turns the Mood and SELECT Activity, from any page; a turn of Activity: Golden's own
tap FX
spin ALGO -1
expect knob0 3
expect knob1 20
spin SELECT 5
expect knob1 25
expect knob0 3
expect tweaks 8
wait 400
spin ALGO -1
expect knob0 2
# Koi: Rain on the Pond (the moods as the day meets them: Natural, Feeding, Rain, Still Pond, Night): the water is the
# recorded rain (the eighth of its list), sparse
spin PRESET 1
wait 1200
expect scene 1
spin K1 2
expect knob0 2
expect knob9 7
expect knob1 15
# rain seen landing on the pond, and heard where it lands
wait 15000
expect rainnow >90
expect raindrops >20
expect knob13 30
# Hotaru: Mist, then Rain (Nature, KNOB 2); the filter deepens with them; glints heard on a clear night
spin PRESET 1
wait 1200
expect scene 2
tap FX
tap FX
tap FX
spin K1 2
expect knob13 2
wait 60000
expect wx 1
expect depthsent >20
spin K1 1
expect knob13 3
# (rain "keeps falling" on switching back) a weather chosen by hand comes in a few seconds
# a few drops first, each on its own, then more
wait 2000
expect dropson <8
wait 4000
expect rainnow >95
# (photos: 33 fps in rain) the drops step every other frame, and only what changed is sent, not
# the blocks across from it: well under a quarter of the screen a frame (~60 %)
expect sentavg >-1
wait 5000
expect sentavg <25
expect dropson >30
wait 54000
expect wx 2
spin K1 -2
expect knob13 1
wait 6000
expect rainnow <5
wait 114000
expect wx 0
expect depthsent 0
expect pings >0
# a mood sets the weather too: Dusk (the first, as the night meets them) is a clear night. Natural keeps the weather turned by hand (its
# tweak: Clear) until it is reset to Auto, as made
tap FX
spin K1 1
expect knob0 0
expect resetm 0
spin K1 1
expect knob0 1
expect knob13 1
spin K1 -1
expect knob0 0
expect knob13 1
expect resetm 0
wait 2500
expect knob13 0
expect tweaks 0
expect stale 0
expect race 0
